From 41891eeb28652b357c7ba0a34733347d36733722 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MangMax <hi@mang.zone>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:41:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: guard article detail mapping against null response
 fields

The article detail mapping assumed every nested field deserialized from the
article page state and the metadata API was present. Real responses can omit
optional or partial data, which produced NullReferenceException in
ArticleAdapter.ToArticleDetail and BuildHtmlContent and made the reader fail
after a successful network round-trip.

- treat readInfo and author as required, failing with an identifiable
  KernelException instead of a NullReferenceException;
- treat metadata stats, like/favorite/attention as optional (nullable counts);
- skip null text nodes, null word nodes, picture/line paragraphs without
  payload and unknown paragraph types while preserving supported paragraph,
  image and line markup exactly;
- reject an empty or unsupported body with a KernelException instead of
  returning an empty article as success.

Adds a kernel-local xUnit project with desensitized structured fixtures that
exercise the real adapter and source-generated deserialization. Red on
0ae5e4e: 9 failed / 3 passed; green: 12 passed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
